# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (preset tsan, .github/workflows/tsan.yml). Only Gothar's own code is instrumented; the
# vcpkg libraries are not, so TSan cannot see their synchronisation and may report races inside them. Suppress those
# by library only - never a race in engine/, game/ or tools/ code.
race:JPH::
race:SDL_
deadlock:JPH::

# miniaudio (header compiled into engine/audio, so instrumented): the spatializer and listener parameters (position,
# direction, world up, cone ...) are plain floats that the setters write on the main thread and the audio thread
# reads while mixing - miniaudio's design, not a lock we skipped. A torn read costs one buffer of slightly wrong
# panning.
race:ma_spatializer_

# The crash handler (engine/platform/src/CrashHandler.cpp) formats and writes its report inside the signal handler
# (allocations, stdio). Not async-signal-safe by intent: the process is dying anyway, and the report is best
# effort (docs/modules/release.md part B). The crash test then sees TSan's report instead of ours.
signal:CrashHandler.cpp
